    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17443653_3651cf7b",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T05:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we move the old data? Can\u0027t we just use a circular buffer instead? (using erased space as end/start indicators).",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "320f0b6e_9c98c335",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-17T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think moving data simplifies log management, also, note that you need to erase the entire page anyways, so a portion of the log needs to be re-written in any case.",
      "parentUuid": "17443653_3651cf7b",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21805416_267e0663",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T04:15:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, it was my first reaction as well (the benefit is we can retain more unread entries when we reach the full log: 100% of its size instead of 25%). but if we do circular buffer, we\u0027ll have to erase \u0026 rewrite the log page in flash on every addition of the new log entry, instead of doing erase only when we are compacting. which may not be great for flash wear - not sure if that\u0027s a concern.",
      "parentUuid": "320f0b6e_9c98c335",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5c73a10_431ed465",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T14:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "both wear and time - writing a few bytes of the new record is much faster than erasing the page and rewriting it.\n\nThe main idea of this is that the log grows very slow and is polled by the host often, so there is no harm in dropping old entries.",
      "parentUuid": "21805416_267e0663",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
