    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ee71b13_3972dd0a",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T05:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t usually use callbacks (for one thing, they make the static stack analysis harder to manage).\n\nI\u0027d either use a weak function that is overridden in the chip/ directory, or a config option (where the function can be defined as an inline no-op if the config is not set). I think we tend to prefer the former for this use case.",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d329d70f_ea0a81b5",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-17T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure who \u0027we\u0027 is in this case, Cr50 code uses callbacks.\n\nI personally think this makes it easier to follow the code than to try figuring out who and when overrides weak functions. This particular callback will not affect stack use analysis. \n\nLet\u0027s see what others think.",
      "parentUuid": "4ee71b13_3972dd0a",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9922d226_b6fad8bc",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T05:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIRC not all EC have their flash directly addressable this way, so you may need to use flash_physical_read instead.",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fcc7b09_bd8df25e",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-17T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "which ones don\u0027t have direct access, is there a config option for this? I would rather use direct access where possible to speed up things.",
      "parentUuid": "9922d226_b6fad8bc",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "036a3a27_e3fe2b29",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T05:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Be careful that some chips have CONFIG_FLASH_WRITE_SIZE !\u003d 1, and your code might not work then. In some cases, CONFIG_FLASH_WRITE_SIZE \u003e 8, so you\u0027ll need to write header and data in one go.\n\nAt the very least, make sure to add BUILD_ASSERT to prevent this code from being used on such chips.",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b262c987_c56f8ac0",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-17T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "good catch, I did not know there were flash cases with write size larger than 4. \n\nNote that this function is guaranteed to be called with padded size, it\u0027s just write sizes larger than the log header structure are not supported by this code. Added a build assert for this in the .h file.",
      "parentUuid": "036a3a27_e3fe2b29",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
